## Installation

### Fork and Forget

Just drop the single `compose.mk` file into your project and use it directly.  No global install, and no dependencies beyond `make` + `bash` (plus `docker` for the container features).

```bash
# Download into your project and make it executable
$ curl -sL \
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Robot-Wranglers/compose.mk/main/compose.mk \
    > compose.mk
$ chmod +x compose.mk
 
# Stand-alone "tool mode"
# Or, from your project Makefile:  `include compose.mk`
$ ./compose.mk <target>     
```

### Global Install

Prefer it **globally, on your `PATH`**?  That's supported with several different installer shims.  Pick your package manager:

| Via | Install |
| --- | --- |
| {{macros.repo_link('via/basher', name='basher', github=github)}} | `basher install Robot-Wranglers/compose.mk` |
| {{macros.repo_link('via/pip', name='pip', github=github)}} | `pip install "git+https://github.com/Robot-Wranglers/compose.mk.git#subdirectory=via/pip"` |
| {{macros.repo_link('via/npm', name='npm', github=github)}} | `npm install -g ./via/npm` *(from a checkout)* |
| {{macros.repo_link('via/docker', name='docker', github=github)}} | `docker build -t compose.mk "https://github.com/Robot-Wranglers/compose.mk.git#main:via/docker"` *(runs from a container; or `docker pull ghcr.io/robot-wranglers/compose.mk`)* |

See the [Quickstart]({{mkdocs.config.site_url}}/quickstart) for tighter project integration and the [compatibility notes]({{mkdocs.config.site_url}}/quickstart/#compatibility-notes).

